course: dictionary
lesson: 2376
title: Words from long ago
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to old times, like castles, kings and Bible stories. You may not hear them at school or at home, but they still appear in books. Context helps: the words around a word show you what job it does.
explain: «In prison Joseph helped the other prisoners and explained the dreams of Pharaoh's baker and cupbearer.» Pharaoh is a king, and a baker makes bread. The cupbearer is listed next to the baker, so it must be another servant in the king's house.
explain: Ask what kind of person would fit there. A cupbearer gives the king his drink, so it fits a trusted servant who works close to the king. Then try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have a good guess, and you can check it in a dictionary.
fact: A cupbearer is a servant who pours and serves wine to a king.
fact: The word comes from two words: cup and bearer, the one who carries the cup.
fact: In old royal courts, a cupbearer often tasted the wine first to check it was not poisoned.
fact: A cupbearer was trusted and stood very close to the king.
fact: In the Bible story of Joseph, Pharaoh's cupbearer and baker had dreams while in prison, and Joseph explained them.
exercise: What does a cupbearer do? | *Pours and serves wine to the king | Bakes bread for the royal feast | Cleans the stables and feeds the horses | Guards the castle gates at night
exercise: «Joseph explained the dreams of Pharaoh's baker and cupbearer.» Which words show that a cupbearer is a job in the royal household? | *Pharaoh and baker | Joseph and prison | Explained and helped | Dreams and night
exercise: Why did a cupbearer often taste the wine first? | *To check it was not poisoned | To make it sweeter for the king | To pay the other servants first | To decide whether it was red or white
test: Which word best describes a cupbearer? | A prisoner who tells dreams | A soldier who guards the king | *A trusted servant of the king | A farmer who grows grapes
test: In the sentence «Pharaoh's cupbearer had a dream in prison», what does cupbearer tell you about the man? | He was a poor farmer | *He was a servant close to the king | He was a king's enemy | He was a visitor from another land
exam: Which meaning of cupbearer fits «Joseph explained the dreams of Pharaoh's baker and cupbearer»? | *A trusted royal servant who pours the king's wine | A king's soldier with a sword | A cook who makes sweet cakes | A prisoner who sold his dreams
